NAME:
  cmu.exe - CodeMeter Universal Support Tool.
  Version 8.40a of 2025-Oct-01(Build 7120) for Win64

SYNOPSIS:
  cmu.exe [ command ] [ options ] 

DESCRIPTION:
  This application is a user command line tool. It should help the user
  to list the CmContainer contents, run a simple framework CmBox test
  and execute some maintenance operations like 'time update' or 'CmFAS'.

COMMANDS:
  /h 
  --help
        Shows this help.
  /v
  --version
        Shows all component version information if available.
  /l
  --list
        Lists all connected CmContainer (serial no. only)
  /x
  --list-content
        Lists the contents of all connected CmContainers.
        To add enabling information add --enabling.
  /k
  --list-server
        Lists all available CmLAN network servers.
  --list-cmready
        Lists all connected CmReady devices.
  /n
  --list-network
        Lists the network license information of the own server.
        --list-network [--server <servername>|--all-servers] [--serial <serial>] [--firmcode <firmcode> [--productcode <productcode> [--featuremap <featuremap>]]] [--show-expiration]
              Lists network license information also of remote CodeMeter server.
        --all-servers
              Lists the network license information for all found servers.
        --server <servername>
              Lists the network license information for the specified server <servername>.
        --show-expiration
              Shows the date when a set Expiration Time or a started Usage Period expires.
        --serial <serial>
        --firmcode <firmcode>
        --productcode <productcode>
        --featuremap <featuremap>
              Specified parameter configure the output according to criteria selected.
  --add-server
        Adds a server to the end of your server search list. As argument,
        pass the server name, IP, broadcast address (255.255.255.255) or
        CmWAN url. Examples:
        server.example.com
        192.0.2.42
        2001:db8::2a
        255.255.255.255
        https://user:secretpassword@server.example.com/cmwan
  --delete-server
        Deletes a server from the server search list. As argument,
        pass the server's name, IP, broadcast address (255.255.255.255)
        or CmWan url as listed.
  --clear-serversearchlist
        Deletes all entries from the server search list. To reactivate
        automatic server broadcast, please add broadcast using option
        "--add-server 255.255.255.255".
  --show-serversearchlist
        Shows the entries in the server search list.
  /c <FI>
  --context <FI>
        Used to request a license update (CmFAS). It creates
        a remote update context file for FirmItem <FI>.
        Option --file specifies the output file or stdout if empty.
  /i
  --import
        Imports a received CmFAS license update to an available CodeMeter 
        license.
        Use option --file to specify the filename to use.
        Use --server to specify the CmLAN server if you want to import the
        update on a remote server.
        Use option --device-id 0x<128 hex digits> with WibuCmLiF files for
        Binding Extension/UFC.
        Use option --cmready-device <device name> with WibuCmLiF files for
        import on a CmReady Device. CmReady Devices can be listed with
        --list-cmready.
  --import-namelist
        Imports a namelist in CodeMeter. Use option --file to specify the
        file to use.
  --show-namelist-hashes
        Reads a file containing a namelist (as of --import-namelist) and
        prints a tab-separated table where the first column contains the
        names and the second their corresponding hashes. Use option --file
        to specify the file to use.
  /d
  --firmware-update
        Starts a CmDongle firmware update. The option --password
        is required if you changed the CmDongle's password.
        /f: manually set path to local update file
  /u
  --time-update
        Starts an update of the certified time for each connected
        CmContainer.
  --add-timeserver
        Appends a single CodeMeter Time Server to your Time Server list. As argument,
        pass the Server name or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6).
  --delete-timeserver
        Deletes a single CodeMeter Time Server from your Time Server list. As argument,
        pass the Server name or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6).
  --set-timeserver-default
        Sets the CodeMeter Time Server settings to default parameters.
        CodeMeter Time Servers: cmtime.codemeter.com, cmtime.codemeter.de, cmtime.codemeter.us
        Timeout: 20 seconds
        Protocol: http
  --show-timeserver-info
        Shows the entries in the CodeMeter Time Server list.
  --set-timeserver-timeout
        Sets the timeout of the CodeMeter Time Server in seconds.
        Value range is between 1 und 120. Default value is 20 seconds.
  --set-timeserver-protocol
        Sets one of the protocols (http or https) for CodeMeter Time Server.
  /e <s>
  --enable <s>
        Allows you to enable or disable the selected CmDongle.
        The UIK password must be specified. The  required new enabling state
        must be defined as parameter <s>
        where s = {1 (disable), 2 (temp. enable), 3 (enable)}
  /t <no>
  --test <no>
        Starts for each connected CmDongle some simple
        tests. The number of tests must be defined as parameter <no>.
        The CmDongle must be (temporarily) enabled.
  /vv
  --cmdust
        Creates a CmDust report. This report is required for support issues.
        It is recommended to create a CmDust report before you contact
        Wibu-Systems support.
        With option --file the result can be written to a text file.
  --borrow 
        Borrows a license from a license
        server to your local computer. You have to specify firmcode
        and productcode of the license using the options --firmcode and
        --productcode. As additional option you can specify the featuremap
        with --featuremap. Furthermore you have to indicate The serial number
        of the client's CmContainer and the server name using --serial
        and --server. If you want to borrow this License for a shorter time
        than set on server side, you may add the parameter --minutes followed
        by the number of minutes you want to use the license.
  --return 
        Returns a borrowed license to the license server. You have to specify
        a Firm Code and Product Code of the license using the options
        --firmcode and --productcode and the serial number of the client's
        CmContainer.
  --borrowlist 
        Creates a listing of the Borrow-Client and Borrow-Server licenses on
        the CmLAN network.
  --transferlist 
        Creates a listing of the license transfer relevant data.
  --enabling 
        Creates a listing of the enabling settings of all connected CmContainers.
        Combined with -x it will add enabling information to the box content.
  --enable-context 
        Shows the enable context of a ProductItem. Use --serial, --firmcode and
        --productcode to specify the requested entry.
  --create-io 
        Used in combination with --file. Only useful for CmCard/SD or
        CmCard/CF. It creates a new codemtr.io file. Call this option only if
        your codemtr.io file has been deleted.
        Typical, call with option: --file F:
  --detect-proxy
        Prints the system proxy to standard output.
  --del
  --delete-cmact-license
        Deletes the CmActLicense specified by --serial.
        Note: Deletion is permanent, the license cannot be restored.
        This works for both CmActLicense Firm Codes and Universal Firm Codes.
        In the latter case, it corresponds to --lt-cleanup --container.
  --delete-cmcloud-credentials
        Deletes the CodeMeter Cloud credentials of the CmCloudContainer
        specified with the  --serial command.
        Note: If you delete the credentials, you can no longer access your
        CmCloudContainer. The license within CodeMeter Cloud however is not
        affected by this action.
  --set-access-data
        Sets Webadmin write authentication. Use with option --password to
        define write password.
  --reset-access-data
        Resets Webadmin authentication. "Local Access only" will be set.
  --set-proxy
        Sets CodeMeter proxy configuration. As argument pass '--use-system-proxy' or the proxy server (name or IP address).
        A port different to the default port (80) may be defined by --port followed by the port number.
        A user password authentication may be set by --username <name of the user> --password <password>.
        To remove the authentication use --username followed by "".

        Examples:
        cmu --set-proxy proxy.company.com --username johndoe --password mypassword --port 70
        cmu --set-proxy proxy.company.com --username ""
        cmu --set-proxy --use-system-proxy
  --show-system-proxy
        Show current system proxy
  --show-codemeter-proxy
        Show current proxy set for CodeMeter in CodeMeter Profiling
  --set-config-disk <parameter>
        Enable you to set special behavior for the virtual flash partition
        like BootCode or Removable flags. (CmStick only)
        Please note, that you must unplug and re-insert the CmStick.
        parameter = {RemovableDisk,LocalDisk}
        parameter = {Int18Boot,ZeroBoot,LoopBoot,SwapBoot,VbrBoot}
        parameter = {ActivePartition,InactivePartition}
        parameter = {Fat16,Fat32}
        parameter = {HidCommunication,MsdCommunication}
        parameter = {LinkPowerManagementOn,LinkPowerManagementOff}
          Remark on Parameter LinkPowerManagementOff:
          By deactivating Link Power Management, the conformity according to USB-IF,
          Errata for USB 2.0 ECN: Link Power Management (LPM), as well as the USB 3.1
          Specification, section 8.5 and 9, is no longer guaranteed. The manufacturer
          hereby excludes any warranty with regards to the function and behaviour of
          the product in relation to these requirements.
          LinkPowerManagementOff can be combined with option --yes to disable
          interactive confirmation.
  --hid
        Sets the USB communication standard to the Human Interface Device (HID)
        class specification.
        Shortcut for --set-config-disk HidCommunication.
        May be used with or without specifying a serial number via --serial.
        Without specifying the command will be executed for all connected
        dongles.
  --msd
        Sets the USB communication standard to the Mass Storage Device (MSD)
        class specification.
        Shortcut for --set-config-disk MsdCommunication.
        May be used with or without specifying a serial number via --serial.
        Without specifying the command will be executed for all connected
        dongles.
  --show-config-disk
        Show current settings like removable/fixed disk or the type of the
        defined master boot record boot code. This options concern the
        behavior of the virtual flash partitions. Useful only for
        CmStick/M or CmCard.
  --create-lt-context <parameters>
        Creates a license transfer context
        Specify the license tranfser type with one of the parameters:
          --lt-fsb (default), --lt-push, --lt-return
        Additional parameters:
          --lt-request-file <file>
              is a mandatory parameter
              It is used to specify the file <file> where the result of the
               license context creation should be written
          --serial <serial> or -s <serial>
              selects the CmContainer with the specified Serial Number
          --firmcode <fc>
              sets the Firm Code to create the context of
          --productcode <pc>
              sets the Product Code of the transferred license.
  --create-lt-update <parameters>
        Enables to transfer a license transfer context. Used with one of
        the following parameters to specify the nature of the transfer:
          --lt-move-licenses <licenses> (the specified number of licenses will
            be transferred)
          --lt-borrow-local-license <expiration time>
            expiration time as YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss
            (one license will be transferred for the specified time limit)
          --lt-return
            return licenses transferred with --lt-move-* or --lt-borrow-*
          --lt-history-index <index> (redo transfer for same target
            without consuming additional units/licenses)
        Additional mandatory parameters:
          --lt-request-file <file>
            is a mandatory parameter
            It is used to specify the file <file> containing the license
            context to be transferred
          --lt-update-file <file>
            is a mandatory parameter
            It is used to specify the file <file> where the result of the
            license transfer should be written
          --serial <serial> or -s <serial>
            selects the CmContainer with the specified Serial Number
          --firmcode <fc>
            sets the Firm Code of the transferred license
          --productcode <pc>
            sets the Product Code of the transferred license
        Additional optional parameters:
          --lt-feature-code <number>
            It is used to specify the Feature Code <number>. The default input
            for the <number> is in decimal unless it begins with 0x or 0X
          --lt-product-ref <number>
            It is used to specify the Product Item Reference <number>. The
            default input for the <number> is in decimal unless it begins
            with 0x or 0X
  --import-lt-update <parameters>
        Updates license transfer data on the target side.
        Further parameters:
          --lt-update-file <file>
            is a mandatory parameter
            It is used to specify the file <file> containing the update
  --create-lt-receipt <parameters>
        Creates a signature with a defined private key and gives it back as a
        receipt.
          --lt-receipt-file <file>
            is a mandatory parameter
            It is used to specify the file <file> where the receipt
            will be written to
          --serial <serial> or -s <serial>
            selects the CmContainer with the specified Serial Number
          --firmcode <fc>
            sets the Firm Code to create the receipt of
  --import-lt-receipt <parameters>
        Checks the receipt with a defined public key confirming the validity
        of a transaction.
          --lt-receipt-file <file>
            is a mandatory parameter
            It is used to specify the file <file> containing the receipt
          --serial <serial> or -s <serial>
            selects the CmContainer with the specified Serial Number
          --firmcode <fc>
            sets the target Firm Code of the import
  --lt-cleanup <parameters>
        Possible cleanup action:
          --deleted: clean deleted licenses
          --disabled:  clean disabled (dangerous)
          --hiddenhistory: clean history of given product item.
          --container: removes whole license container (dangerous)
        Arguments:
          --serial <serial> or -s <serial>
            selects the container by serial number
          --firmcode <fc>
            selects license by firm code 
          --productcode <pc>
            selects product by product code 
          --lt-product-ref <number>
            needed for mode disabled or deleted
            It is used to specify the Product Item Reference <number>. The
            default input for the <number> is in decimal unless it begins
            with 0x or 0X
  --list-rejected-allocations <subcommand>!
        List rejected license allocations. This feature may be activated 
        and deactivated either via cmu or CodeMeter-Profiling. Querying the 
        current status of the feature or retrieving any gathered data (if 
        available) is possible at all times.
        Available subcommands:
          --activate <optional parameters>:
              Activate this feature to track all rejected license allocations.
              Further (optional) parameters:
                --firmcode <fc>
                  Only track the specificed firmcode (Default = All).
                --max-entries <num>
                  Manually configure the maximum number of entries to hold
                  until retrieval (Default = 1000).
          --deactivate:
            Deactivate this feature.
            Already gathered data may still be retrieved afterwards via the 
            '--get-data' mode.
          --get-data <optional parameters>:
            Retrieve gathered data.
            Further (optional) parameters:
              --file <filename>
                Write (append) data to file instead of printing to stdout.
          --status:
            Print current feature status.
  --export-acl
        Export License Access Permissions (Access Control List) to file.
        Use option --file to specify the filename to use.
  --import-acl
        Import License Access Permissions (Access Control List) from file.
        Use option --file to specify the filename to use.
  --verify-cloud-connection
        Tries to contact the cloud at the url:  https://eu-backend.wibu.cloud/test.
        To customize the url use the option --url.
  --set-diagnose-level <level>
        Sets the diagnose level persistently. Available diagnose levels are:
        1 = error
        2 = warning
        3 = info
        4 = debug

OPTIONS:
  /f <file>
  --file <file> 
        Additional option to specify that the result of a command should
        be written to file <file>. Option is useful in combination with
        --context, --import, --cmdust.
  /s <serial>
  --serial <serial> 
        Additional option to specify that a selected command should only
        work on the CmContainer with the specified Serial Number
        <serial> i.e. "1-10234242".
  /p <pwd>
  --password <pwd> 
        In combination with --enable and --firmware-update, this option
        sets the UIK password to use for the command.
        In combination with --set-access-data, this option
        defines the write password for WebAdmin write authentication.
  /y
  --yes 
        Assume "yes" as the answer to all prompts and run non-interactively
  --firmcode <fc> 
        In combination with --borrow or --return or the license transfer
        functions, this option sets the Firm Code of the borrowed or transferred
        license.
  --productcode <pc> 
        In combination with --borrow or --return, this option sets the
        Product Code of the borrowed license.
  --featuremap <fm> 
        In combination with --borrow or --return, this option sets the
        Feature Map of the borrowed license.
  --server <servername> 
        Additional option to borrow a license from a specific server.
        Used with --borrow
  --minutes <minutes> 
        Additional option to borrow a license for a specific amount of
        minutes. It is not possible to enhance the borrow period by this option.
        Used with --borrow
  --url <url> 
        optional in combination with --verify-cloud-connection to specify
        another url.

Feature: named user license
        username and domain are set automatically
        see cmu --version for detected values
  --nmu-userdefined <text>
        utf-8 string (case sensitive!) truncated after 127 bytes

EXAMPLES:
  cmu.exe  --version
       Show version of running CodeMeter components.
  cmu.exe  --cmdust --file <file>
       Create CmDust diagnostic support report, write result to file.
  cmu.exe  --list-server --list-content
       List all available CmLAN network servers and if available
       a list of connected CodeMeter licenses on it.
  cmu.exe  --test 100 --serial 1-233232
       Start 100 simple test of CmDongle. Test will run only with
       CmDongle with Serial Number 1-233232.
  cmu.exe  --import --file 1-232323.WibuCmRaU
       Import the given CmFAS update file.
  cmu.exe  --enable 2 --serial 1-2345 --password SECRET
       Change enabling state to "temp. enabled" for the CmDongle 1-2345
       and use the UIK password "SECRET".

